00:28:41.150 --> 00:28:42.630
I'm going to go check on my cat.
我要回去看看我的猫。

627
00:28:42.750 --> 00:28:43.170
I know.
我知道。

628
00:28:43.450 --> 00:28:45.850
But yeah, she kind of felt peer pressure a little bit.
不过确实，她当时多少有点迫于同辈压力。

629
00:28:46.090 --> 00:28:51.450
I mean, I think it's fair to say that both Pam and Dwight contributed to Sprinkles' death,
我的意思是，说帕姆和德怀特都对小饼干的死负有责任算得上公允，

630
00:28:51.450 --> 00:28:55.570
but then also maybe Meredith did by getting hit by the car in the first place.
但话说回来，也许梅雷迪思自己也有责任，谁让她一开始就被车撞了呢。

631
00:28:55.570 --> 00:28:57.050
Well, then we need to point to Michael.
那我们还得怪到迈克尔头上。

632
00:28:57.650 --> 00:28:58.210
Exactly.
没错。

633
00:28:58.250 --> 00:29:00.590
This goes, this trail goes back.
这个，这条线索可以追溯回去。

634
00:29:00.610 --> 00:29:03.670
Maybe it's all the way to Michael for creating this moment.
说不定得一路追溯到迈克尔头上，是他制造了这一幕。

635
00:29:04.150 --> 00:29:04.730
Kind of true.
倒也实话。

636
00:29:05.450 --> 00:29:06.250
All right.
好了。

637
00:29:06.450 --> 00:29:07.910
Fan theory number two.
粉丝理论之二。

638
00:29:08.190 --> 00:29:08.850
Oh my gosh.
噢天哪。

639
00:29:09.030 --> 00:29:11.450
This was also a fan mail flurry.
这也是一波粉丝来信热潮。

640
00:29:12.250 --> 00:29:18.230
People would like us to discuss, are garbage and bandit the same cat just renamed?
大家想让我们讨论一下，“垃圾”和“强盗”其实是同一只猫，只是改了个名字？

641
00:29:18.230 --> 00:29:20.210
From Alpha M in Utah.
来自犹他州的阿尔法·M。

642
00:29:20.910 --> 00:29:28.970
In Dunder Mifflin Infinity Part 1, Dwight releases a cat that he had trapped for Angela named Garbage.
在《邓德米夫林无限公司》上集里，德怀特放生了一只他为安吉拉捉来的名叫“垃圾”的猫。

643
00:29:29.090 --> 00:29:30.990
Tries to win you over with Garbage.
试图用“垃圾”来赢得你的芳心。

644
00:29:31.150 --> 00:29:35.850
He releases this cat down in the warehouse area.
他在仓库区放生了这只猫。

645
00:29:36.110 --> 00:29:36.530
Okay.
好吧。

646
00:29:36.530 --> 00:29:46.190
And then in Money Part 2, Andy gives Angela a cat that he found in the warehouse in this same general area.
然后在《钱》下集里，安迪送给安吉拉一只他在仓库区同一片大致区域找到的猫。

647
00:29:46.890 --> 00:29:53.150
So the theory goes that Garbage is the same cat.
所以这种理论认为，“垃圾”就是同一只猫。

648
00:29:53.150 --> 00:30:00.970
So basically they're saying the cat that Dwight released into the warehouse and then the cat that Andy brings to Angela are one in the same.
所以基本上他们的意思是，德怀特放生到仓库的猫和安迪带给安吉拉的猫是同一只。

649
00:30:01.130 --> 00:30:01.510
Yes.
对。

650
00:30:01.770 --> 00:30:08.970
But then the cat that Angela gets from Andy is the same cat that lives in her drawer that then goes in the ceiling.
但接着安吉拉从安迪那里得到的猫，就是那只住在她抽屉里、后来又爬进天花板的猫。

651
00:30:08.970 --> 00:30:10.710
So that must be bandit.
所以那只肯定就是班迪特。

652
00:30:10.710 --> 00:30:17.630
So the question is, from Gen B in Crawford, Georgia, Garbage is Bandit, right?
所以问题是，来自佐治亚州克劳福德的Gen B认为垃圾猫就是班迪特，对吧？

653
00:30:18.130 --> 00:30:19.790
Was the same cat used?
用的是同一只猫吗？

654
00:30:20.110 --> 00:30:22.290
Well, no, the same cat was not used.
嗯，没有，没有用同一只猫。

655
00:30:22.530 --> 00:30:27.190
The cat that played Garbage is not the same cat that played Bandit.
扮演垃圾猫的猫和扮演班迪特的猫不是同一只。

656
00:30:27.470 --> 00:30:31.310
However, we did talk about this in our breakdown of Money Part 2.
不过，我们在解析《金钱》（下）时确实讨论过这个。

657
00:30:31.750 --> 00:30:38.830
And you and I agreed, Angela, that we think that Garbage is the cat that Andy trapped and gave to Angela.
安吉拉，你和我当时都同意，我们认为垃圾猫就是安迪设陷阱抓住并送给安吉拉的那只猫。

658
00:30:39.350 --> 00:30:42.210
We agreed that she renamed him Bandit.
我们一致认为她把它重新命名为班迪特。

659
00:30:42.530 --> 00:30:42.970
Yes.
是的。

660
00:30:43.130 --> 00:30:46.710
We followed the logic that this is the same cat that was in the warehouse.
我们顺着这个逻辑，认为这就是仓库里的那只猫。

661
00:30:47.210 --> 00:30:47.550
Yes.
没错。

662
00:30:47.670 --> 00:30:47.830
Yeah.
对。

663
00:30:47.930 --> 00:30:48.650
I remember that.
我记得那个。

664
00:30:48.810 --> 00:30:56.170
And then I think I shared this, but just for everyone to know, the cat that played Garbage was one of the biggest cats I've ever held in my life.
然后我想我分享过这个，但为了让大家知道，扮演垃圾猫的那只猫是我这辈子抱过的最大的一只猫。

665
00:30:56.270 --> 00:30:57.110
It was so huge.
它太巨大了。

666
00:30:57.310 --> 00:30:58.170
It was so big.
它真的好大。

667
00:30:58.350 --> 00:30:58.610
Yes.
对。

668
00:30:58.770 --> 00:31:02.690
And I don't think I could have put that cat up in the same case.
而且我觉得我不可能把那只猫塞进同一个天花板夹层里。

669
00:31:02.690 --> 00:31:08.890
Because, so that's the question, which is like, was it intended to be the same cat?
因为，问题就在这里，就像是，本来就打算当成同一只猫吗？

670
00:31:09.310 --> 00:31:12.330
Like, is this theory like what was intended?
比如说，这个理论符合原本的意图吗？

671
00:31:12.770 --> 00:31:18.270
And did we just switch cats because you couldn't physically throw the original cat up into the ceiling?
我们换猫是不是因为你体力上根本没办法把原本的那只猫往上扔进天花板？

672
00:31:18.270 --> 00:31:19.410
We had to recast?
我们不得不重新选角？

673
00:31:19.630 --> 00:31:22.050
Or was it like, we don't know.
还是说，我们也不知道。

674
00:31:22.170 --> 00:31:23.050
Yeah, we don't know.
对，我们不知道。

675
00:31:23.150 --> 00:31:24.270
Except I do agree.
不过我确实同意。

676
00:31:24.430 --> 00:31:27.290
I think that Garbage is Bandit, that Angela renames it.
我认为垃圾猫就是班迪特，是安吉拉给它改了名。

677
00:31:27.290 --> 00:31:31.510
I also think Angela would never, ever call a cat Garbage.
我也觉得安吉拉绝对、绝对不会叫一只猫“垃圾”。

678
00:31:31.790 --> 00:31:40.930
So if she was given that cat again from Andy and she's trying to be spiteful to Dwight and this time she's taking the cat, even though it was the same cat,
所以如果安迪再次把那只猫送给她，而她正想对德怀特恶毒一把，这次她把猫收下了，哪怕它是同一只猫，

679
00:31:41.110 --> 00:31:42.870
she would rename it for sure.
她也肯定会给它改名。

680
00:31:43.150 --> 00:31:50.150
Well, I went back and I watched this part of the episode where Angela discovers this cat in a box on her desk.
嗯，我回去重看了这一集里安吉拉发现办公桌上的盒子里的这只猫的那个片段。

681
00:31:50.150 --> 00:32:01.210
There's a look that she shares with Dwight when she receives the cat, but then thanks Andy for it.
当她收到这只猫时，她和德怀特交换了一个眼神，然后为此感谢了安迪。

682
00:32:01.430 --> 00:32:05.050
And then Dwight's face just falls.
接着德怀特的脸一下子就垮了。

683
00:32:05.270 --> 00:32:06.770
He's so sad.
他太难过了。

684
00:32:07.210 --> 00:32:12.470
And I think that she knows it's the cat he gave her.
我觉得她知道这就是他送给她的那只猫。

685
00:32:12.610 --> 00:32:12.930
Yeah.
对。

686
00:32:13.070 --> 00:32:15.210
And now Andy's getting credit for it.
现在安迪却因此受到了表扬。

687
00:32:15.530 --> 00:32:15.730
Yeah.
是啊。

688
00:32:15.930 --> 00:32:19.390
Like she wouldn't accept it from Dwight, but she'll accept it from Andy.
就像她不会接受德怀特的，但她会接受安迪的。

689
00:32:19.390 --> 00:32:21.410
And it's like this extra dagger.
这就好比又补了一刀。

690
00:32:21.930 --> 00:32:31.250
Yeah, because you would have to know, and Dwight would have to know, how much willpower it would take for Angela not to accept a cat from anyone.
对，因为你肯定知道，德怀特也肯定知道，安吉拉要克制住不接受任何人的猫，需要付出多大的意志力。

691
00:32:31.650 --> 00:32:32.170
Correct.
没错。

692
00:32:32.890 --> 00:32:33.390
All right.
好了。

693
00:32:33.430 --> 00:32:34.670
Well, I enjoyed that discussion.
嗯，我很享受这个讨论。

694
00:32:34.790 --> 00:32:35.290
I did too.
我也是。

695
00:32:35.590 --> 00:32:41.570
Now we're moving into fan theory number three, which is that Angela is not really a vegetarian.
现在我们要进入第三个粉丝理论，也就是安吉拉其实不是真正的素食主义者。

696
00:32:42.310 --> 00:32:42.550
Oh.
哦。

697
00:32:43.870 --> 00:32:46.850
Lady, there is so much conflicting evidence.
天哪，有太多相互矛盾的证据了。

698
00:32:46.850 --> 00:32:49.370
I have a question for you.
我有个问题要问你。

699
00:32:49.570 --> 00:32:50.150
What is it?
什么问题？

700
00:32:50.350 --> 00:32:53.450
Did people bring up the chicken piccata at the hospital?
有没有人提到过医院里的柠檬鸡片？

701
00:32:53.550 --> 00:32:54.070
Okay.
好的。

702
00:32:54.410 --> 00:32:54.570
Yeah.
对。

703
00:32:55.050 --> 00:32:57.170
So it all starts in email surveillance.
所以这一切始于邮件监控。

704
00:32:58.010 --> 00:32:59.210
She's at the barbecue.
她在烧烤派对上。

705
00:32:59.970 --> 00:33:01.450
Jim offers her some barbecue.
吉姆拿烧烤给她吃。

706
00:33:01.450 --> 00:33:04.570
And Angela says, I'm a vegetarian.
安吉拉说，我是个素食主义者。

707
00:33:05.250 --> 00:33:09.270
Then in business ethics, she only eats potato salad.
然后在商业道德那一集里，她只吃土豆沙拉。

708
00:33:09.510 --> 00:33:12.810
This is when Meredith has slept with the rep and has gotten everyone's steak.
当时梅雷迪思和代表睡了，拿到了所有人的牛排。

709
00:33:12.970 --> 00:33:13.350
That's right.
没错。

710
00:33:13.350 --> 00:33:18.810
And then there's other little moments where this idea of her being a vegetarian plays out.
然后还有其他一些小瞬间，体现出她是一个素食主义者。

711
00:33:18.990 --> 00:33:20.730
For example, Kate H.
比如，凯特·H。

712
00:33:21.070 --> 00:33:23.410
from Parkersburg, West Virginia pointed out,
来自西弗吉尼亚州帕克斯堡的她指出，

713
00:33:23.810 --> 00:33:28.890
While watching Dinner Party, I noticed something that is a true testament to the attention to detail in the show.
在看《晚餐派对》时，我注意到了一点，这真正证明了这部剧对细节的关注。

714
00:33:29.170 --> 00:33:34.630
When everyone finally gets their long-awaited dinner, Angela Martin covers the meat on her plate with a napkin.
当大家终于吃上期待已久的晚餐时，安吉拉·马丁用餐巾盖住了盘子里的肉。

715
00:33:34.770 --> 00:33:36.030
I thought it was so cool.
我觉得太酷了。

716
00:33:36.270 --> 00:33:37.590
I improvised that.
那是我即兴发挥的。

717
00:33:37.770 --> 00:33:38.030
Yay!
太棒了！

718
00:33:39.010 --> 00:33:41.150
I just thought she wouldn't want to look at it.
我只是觉得她不想看到那块肉。

719
00:33:41.530 --> 00:33:46.230
Kate said, as a super fan, I know that Angela is a vegetarian, so it came as no surprise.
凯特说，作为一个超级粉丝，我知道安吉拉是个素食主义者，所以这并不奇怪。

720
00:33:46.230 --> 00:33:51.510
But I love when there are little details that are callbacks or support a character's backstory.
但我很喜欢那些前后呼应或者支撑角色背景故事的小细节。

721
00:33:52.130 --> 00:33:55.190
So wonderful support for that character backstory.
对角色背景故事的这种支撑真是太棒了。

722
00:33:56.250 --> 00:34:00.790
But there are a lot of times when Angela seems to not be a vegetarian.
但也有很多时候，安吉拉看起来并不像个素食主义者。

723
00:34:01.770 --> 00:34:06.710
For example, in Money, when Andy asks her out to dinner, she says she'll go,
比如在《钱》那一集里，安迪约她吃晚餐，她说她会去，

724
00:34:06.710 --> 00:34:10.370
but she insists, quote, no vegetables and no seafood.
但她坚持说，引述一下，“不要蔬菜，也不要海鲜”。

725
00:34:10.610 --> 00:34:11.550
What is she eating?
她到底吃什么？

726
00:34:11.810 --> 00:34:16.510
Listen, I have two very good friends who are vegetarians, and they don't like vegetables.
听着，我有两个很好的朋友是素食主义者，他们不喜欢蔬菜。

727
00:34:16.790 --> 00:34:17.470
What do they eat?
他们吃什么？

728
00:34:17.470 --> 00:34:18.330
And they don't like seafood.
而且他们也不喜欢海鲜。

729
00:34:18.550 --> 00:34:19.630
What do they eat?
他们吃什么？

730
00:34:19.710 --> 00:34:26.070
They eat a lot of, like, beans, pastas, but they don't want a Brussels sprout or carrots.
他们吃很多豆类、面食之类的主食，但他们不想吃抱子甘蓝或胡萝卜。

731
00:34:26.110 --> 00:34:27.810
Like, they eat potatoes.
比如，他们吃土豆。

732
00:34:28.470 --> 00:34:31.050
So that wasn't too far off the mark for me.
所以对我来说，这不算太离谱。

733
00:34:31.190 --> 00:34:33.530
She just might not like some vegetables.
她可能只是不喜欢某些蔬菜而已。

734
00:34:33.530 --> 00:34:34.370
Okay.
好吧。

735
00:34:34.750 --> 00:34:38.510
But then, as you mentioned, Angela, how do you explain this one?
但正如你所提到的，安吉拉，你怎么解释这个呢？

736
00:34:38.690 --> 00:34:44.330
In Jury Duty, she says Philip was conceived after, quote, too much wine and chicken piccata.
在《陪审义务》里，她说菲利普是在，引述一下，“喝了太多酒和吃了柠檬汁煎鸡肉”之后怀上的。

737
00:34:44.890 --> 00:34:51.430
And also, in Moving On, she eats the meat stew with Aunt Shirley, which you said she did as a courtesy.
还有，在《继续前进》里，她和雪莉阿姨一起吃肉汤炖菜，你之前说那是出于礼貌。

738
00:34:51.690 --> 00:34:53.870
Yeah, I sort of thought maybe she just had the broth.
对，我当时想也许她只喝了汤。

739
00:34:54.090 --> 00:34:58.370
The one that is the most puzzling to me is the chicken piccata, the wine sauce.
最让我费解的是那个柠檬汁煎鸡肉，还有白酒酱汁。

740
00:34:58.370 --> 00:35:03.650
So, I'm like, did she decide to eat meat when she was pregnant?
所以我在想，难道她怀孕的时候决定吃肉了吗？

741
00:35:04.030 --> 00:35:05.430
Oh, but she wasn't pregnant yet.
哦，但她当时还没怀孕呢。

742
00:35:05.430 --> 00:35:05.790
No.
对。

743
00:35:05.990 --> 00:35:06.130
No.
对。

744
00:35:06.450 --> 00:35:07.730
That's how she got pregnant.
那是她怀上孩子的时候。

745
00:35:07.730 --> 00:35:08.570
That's how she got pregnant.
那是她怀上孩子的时候。

746
00:35:08.730 --> 00:35:11.110
That's the one that's like, that doesn't quite track.
这就是那个有点说不通的地方。

747
00:35:11.730 --> 00:35:12.050
Yeah.
是啊。

748
00:35:12.670 --> 00:35:14.310
Well, listen, why don't we take a break?
好吧，听着，我们为什么不休息一下呢？

749
00:35:14.310 --> 00:35:18.170
And when we come back, we're going to do our All About Angela Martin Q&A.
等我们回来后，我们将进行“走近安吉拉·马丁”问答环节。

750
00:35:18.310 --> 00:35:19.490
I'm so excited about this.
我对此太兴奋了。

751
00:35:19.590 --> 00:35:23.950
You guys wrote in the best questions, and I'm excited to hear the answers.
你们写进来了最棒的问题，我很期待听到答案。

752
00:35:24.190 --> 00:35:24.730
I am, too.
我也是。

753
00:35:25.470 --> 00:35:40.370
We are back, and I'm just so excited to dig into this Q&A section.
我们回来了，我非常激动能深入这个问答环节。

754
00:35:40.850 --> 00:35:49.010
Angela, I think the character that you developed is so just deliciously complex and interesting.
安吉拉，我觉得你塑造这个角色实在是太美妙、太复杂也太有趣了。

755
00:35:49.770 --> 00:35:54.470
She is full of surprises, and she is nothing like you in real life.
她充满了惊喜，而且她在现实生活中跟你一点都不像。

756
00:35:55.050 --> 00:35:59.610
In fact, we got a letter that made me chuckle, and I'd like to start with it.
事实上，我们收到了一封让我忍俊不禁的信，我想从它开始。

757
00:35:59.670 --> 00:35:59.890
Okay.
好的。

758
00:35:59.890 --> 00:36:04.470
It's from Lisa in Calgary, Alberta, who said,
它来自阿尔伯塔省卡尔加里的丽莎，她说，

759
00:36:04.770 --> 00:36:07.790
Not a question, just a cute story for Angela.
不是问题，只是给安吉拉的一个可爱的小故事。

760
00:36:08.430 --> 00:36:13.650
I was telling my mom, a new Office fan, who I got listening to the podcast, too.
我当时正在跟我妈说话，她是一个新晋的《办公室》剧迷，也是我拉进播客听众圈的人。

761
00:36:13.830 --> 00:36:14.650
Thanks, Lisa.
谢谢你，丽莎。

762
00:36:14.910 --> 00:36:16.790
I know, getting us new listeners.
我知道，给我们带来了新听众。

763
00:36:16.990 --> 00:36:17.270
Yeah.
对。

764
00:36:17.550 --> 00:36:22.570
I was telling my mom about the podcast, and my son Liam piped up and said,
我当时在跟我妈聊这个播客，我的儿子利亚姆插话说道，

765
00:36:23.030 --> 00:36:23.890
It is good.
这挺好的。

766
00:36:24.110 --> 00:36:27.310
It's good to know Angela isn't a bee in real life.
很高兴知道安吉拉在现实生活中不是个碧池。

